/P 154 0 R
/E (benjamin lee hicks, PhD \(they/them\) is a visual artist, educational researcher, and elementary school teacher. Their graphic scholarship infuses the process of teacher professional learning with conversations about comic art as pedagogy, arts-based ethnography, contemplative teacher practice, and the importance of activism for equity in education. They received their PhD in Curriculum and Pedagogy from OISE / University of Toronto in June, 2022. Their dissertation is titled, To Do This Discussion Differently: Queering Teacher Professional Learning Through Comic Art and Graphic Stories. In addition to their work in academia and elementary school classrooms, benjamin has been facilitating visual art and creative bookmaking programs in community contexts for the past 25 years. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
