301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Jorie Morrow \(she/her\) is no stranger to Gailey Road Productions. She has performed, Worried mother in Pound Predators, Anita in both Harriet's House and Ana's Shadow. She has also played a number of diverse roles in our production of Out At School. Jorie is a Toronto based actor/producer and loves to dance! For two years she was a guest speaker on Aboriginal Voices Radio, exploring both medical model approaches and indigenous practices in relation to women's mental health. She has produced many indie productions of new works here in the GTA. When not on stage, Jorie is an activist, social worker/therapist working in community mental health. She is a certified mindfulness meditation facilitator for artists and non-artists. In November she will be dancing with the award winning Moonhorse Dance Theatre in Toronto at the Citadel dance theatre. She is writing her own play, just think of the PITT, except set right here in Toronto, in the streets with a team of mental health professionals. To say that she is thrilled to be here today and share in the Gailey Road celebrations is a massive understatement. Love to her dear ones, Bob and Hailee for their ongoing relentless support and inspiration. Her proudest work to date, by far, is her fabulous family. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Kael Reid \(they/them\) is an Assistant Professor in the Faculty of Liberal Arts and Professional Studies at York University, here in Toronto, where they teach core and elective courses in Children, Childhood, and Youth Studies. With a background in music-making and performing, Kael collaborates with young people and adults to help them document their perspectives and stories through songwriting, singing, and recording. In their spare time, Kael loves doing stuff outside and hanging out with their 3 cats.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
