<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (Mary Ellen MacLean \(she/her\) \(a proud East coaster\) is a performer, creator, educator, director, and producer who works in theatres across Canada and abroad. With a strong foundation in physical theatre, movement, character development, and improvisation, Mary Ellen has over three decades of experience in the theatre world. She studied with theatre/mime mentor Tony Montanaro in Maine, USA. She was a founding member of the Halifax physical theatre ensemble, Jest in Time, touring worldwide for twenty years as well as starring in three national CBC television specials. NS Theatre Merritt Awards for Best Production \(Trip\) and Lifetime Achievement \(Jest\). Her one-woman play Frankie toured across Canada and aired on Bravo TV. Her play Velocipede used 21 bicycles, 7 dancers/performers to tell the story of how the bicycle played a role in the emancipation of women as a symbol for freedom. Since 2023 Mary Ellen has been offering ElderQueers Storytelling at The National Arts Centre in Ottawa both in person and online and this past year at Halifax Pride.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (Her artistic journey is fueled by a dedication to helping performers/people discover their unique artistic voice. By blending body, mind, and spirit, Mary Ellen empowers artists to unlock their full potential and express their individuality on stage and beyond. Mary Ellen MacLean is committed to cultivating an atmosphere of creativity, support and most importantly a place to play, push your limits and have fun.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
